## Data Requirements

**Core Entities:**
- **Browser session** (new, server-side): opaque session identifier (cookie value), stable principal ID, issuer, display name, server-held access/refresh/ID tokens, created-at, last-activity-at, absolute expiry, idle expiry, CSRF secret, active knowledge base, grant revision seen. Storage, encryption at rest and table design are Phase B decisions.
- **Principal / Membership** (existing, F0002): read-only here. Memberships carry tenant, knowledge base, role and grant revision.
- **AuthenticationEvent** (existing, F0001/F0002): gains new reason codes for session and throttling outcomes (`rate_limited`, session expiry and revocation-failure reasons); exact codes are Phase B.

**Validation Rules:**
- Return routes are same-origin relative paths that match a registered route pattern; anything else becomes `/` (S0001 AC5).
- The active knowledge base must be one of the principal's current memberships; otherwise it resets to none (S0006 AC4).

**Data Relationships:**
- Browser session → Principal: N:1. A session never changes principal; a different principal at re-authentication ends it (S0004 AC5).

## Role-Based Access

The shell adds no role, resource or grant. Every protected read and write keeps the engine's existing authorization (F0002, ADR-0061/0062); UI guards and hidden controls are convenience only (§120.5).

| Role | Access Level | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| Any verified USER principal with no membership | Sign in, see Home with a "no access yet" state, sign out | First-sight provisioning stays as in F0002 (no grants) |
| TenantMember | Shell, Home, own memberships; reads the engine already allows | Unchanged policy |
| Reviewer | Above, plus the rehosted Review Panel's existing read and decision actions | Unchanged policy; F0022 owns reviewer authority changes |
| Service / agent principals | No browser session; bearer API only | BFF sign-in refused for non-human clients (S0001 AC6) |
| Unauthenticated | Sign-in entry, signed-out page, throttling page | No protected data |

## Success Criteria

- §121.2 items 8 and 9 pass against real authentik and PostgreSQL in the later feature run, which makes ADR-0051 eligible for operator acceptance.
- F0022 and F0023 can mount routes into the shell without changing session, cache or styling choices.
- The rejected-credential burst proof closes the F0002 medium recommendation.

## Risks & Assumptions

**Operator decisions (G1, 2026-11-27):**

| ID | Question | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | Session bounds | Server-enforced 30-minute idle timeout and 8-hour absolute lifetime; idle warning 2 minutes before expiry; after the absolute limit the user signs in again at the IdP with no silent renewal |
| D2 | Shell scope in v0.1 | Sign-in/out, session status, Home with identity and memberships, active knowledge-base selector (narrowing only; switching clears caches), the route/flag/lazy-load seam, and the proof Review Panel rehosted behind the cookie session with the token-in-URL entry removed; its decision submission is the real mutation for §121.2 item 9 |
| D3 | Re-authentication UX | Popup re-authentication keeps in-memory work; blocked mutations are shown as not submitted and need explicit re-confirmation; if the popup is blocked, a full redirect restores only the sanitized route |
| D4 | Rejected-credential throttling | Per client: up to 20 rejected credentials per 60 s each write the normal event; then `429` with `Retry-After`, no per-request row, and one `rate_limited` event per client per window; applies to the bearer API and the BFF cookie path |

**PM assumptions (for operator review at G3):**

- **A1 — Browsers:** the latest two major versions of desktop Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari; layouts work from 360 px wide.
- **A2 — Accessibility:** WCAG 2.2 AA for every F0021 screen, with zero serious or critical axe violations.
- **A3 — Locale:** `en-US` only; all user-facing strings come from translation resources so later locales need no code change.
- **A4 — Non-browser clients:** the bearer-token API stays for service, agent, Neuron and test callers. The BFF is the only browser path; the shell never sends a bearer token.
- **A5 — Idle activity:** only a user-initiated request extends the idle timer. Background session-status checks do not.
- **A6 — Client address for throttling:** the immediate peer address, or a forwarded address only when it comes from a configured trusted proxy.
- **A7 — Active knowledge base:** a narrowing preference held with the server session, so it survives reload, and reset on principal change. It never grants access.
- **A8 — Other tabs:** after logout or session end in one tab, other tabs of the same browser show the signed-out state on their next server call and within 60 seconds.

**Risks:**
- Popup blockers: mitigated by the redirect fallback (D3).
- `Secure` cookies on local `http://localhost`: the local proof profile and TLS approach are Phase B decisions; production ingress is F0026.
- authentik revocation behavior: the upstream-failure path must be forced in the proof (S0009), not assumed.

## Dependencies

- **F0002** (Done): verified principals, memberships, grant revisions, `authentication_event`, authorization execution.
- **F0001-S0004** (Done): the proof Review Panel and its review routes, rehosted unchanged in behavior.
- **F0011** (Done): generated contracts under `experience/src/generated/contracts/v1/` that the shell consumes.
- **Downstream:** F0022, F0023 (mount routes; inherit session and app-wide choices), F0067 (route seam), F0026 (event retention, production ingress).

